# CITATION.cff — makes GitHub's "Cite this repository" button work and feeds
# Zenodo metadata on future mints. The concept DOI below cites the living work
# (always resolves to the latest archived version); cite a version DOI only to
# pin a release (v3.11.6: 10.5281/zenodo.23303470).
#
# NOTE (2026-10-11): the authors list currently carries the human author only.
# The README credits Claude models as co-creators; whether the FORMAL citation
# record lists them is the founder's standing decision (flagged at the first
# mint, Custos brief 1757) — amend here and in the Zenodo record when ruled.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this template or the ADRs4AI methodology, please cite it using
  these metadata. The concept DOI cites the living work; version DOIs pin
  specific releases.
title: "human-ai-collaboration-template-A"
abstract: >-
  The canonical methodology template of the ADRs4AI paradigm: durable
  human-AI collaboration through Architectural Deliberation Records (ADRs),
  seeds, navigation codes, and the ORRCF recommendation form — with the
  deliberation record itself as the proof of method.
authors:
  - family-names: "Lumbroso"
    given-names: "Jérémie"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23303469
repository-code: "https://github.com/ADRs4AI/human-ai-collaboration-template-A"
license: MIT
